IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `fpine-infringements`

-- Fines, Penalties and Infringement Notices Enforcement Act 1994 (WA) -- the Q&A layer: the questions people ask, with
-- the seat and the situation as parameters, so that one deployment serves every seat and the question form drops the
-- questions that do not arise.
--
-- SEATS (`my role`, the first input of every exported question, "Which of these describes you"):
--   * the person given an infringement notice (the Act's "alleged offender", s 11) -- the baseline's seat, whose 23
--     questions are asked here by calling the baseline's functions in fpine-infringements.l4 (the two questions about a
--     court fine's work and development permit are asked of the second seat, and the first seat is told, settled on its
--     role alone, that a permit is not for an infringement notice);
--   * the person fined by a court -- whose fine is a Part 4 fine (s 28(1)): the work and development permit (ss 4A,
--     46A-46C) and, once a warrant issues, what the Sheriff cannot seize (Part 7, s 75, r 8).
-- A question about another role answers `does not arise for you` without reading any other input. The Registrar, the
-- prosecuting authority, the Sheriff and the Magistrates Court are never seats: what they may or must do appears as what
-- it means for the person asking.
--
-- SITUATIONS (design D8 of the graffiti encoding): within a role, a question that arises only in a situation takes that
-- situation's fact straight after `my role`, and when it does not hold answers `does not arise for you` without reading
-- anything else. The questions of one situation share one input, character for character. They are:
--   * for the person given a notice, `the latest document I have been given` (the baseline's `Stage`): Part 3 ties each
--     step to the document before it, so each step's question arises only at the stage the Act ties it to -- a final
--     demand after the notice (s 14), registration after a final demand (s 15), a notice of intention to enforce after an
--     order to pay or elect (s 18), suspension after that notice (s 19), its cancellation once an order is made (ss 20,
--     20A), a warrant after the notice or an order (s 21A), a time to pay order once the notice is registered (s 21B),
--     the Act's election from the final demand on (ss 14(4)(b), 21), and the s 68B, s 101AA and s 75 questions once a
--     warrant has issued. Each helper that reads the stage lists every value, with no OTHERWISE (graffiti finding 31).
--     The refund (s 22(5)(a)) arises only when `the proceedings were withdrawn`, the baseline's own input;
--   * for the person fined by a court, `an enforcement warrant has been issued against me` (s 75);
--   * a question that arises at every stage (does Part 3 apply, the days a step gives, the fees, what I must pay now,
--     whether I am taken to be convicted, the remote-area test, s 24) takes no situation input; the four that need the
--     stage take it as an ordinary input, under the same name.
--
-- No exported question takes a DEONTIC or EVENT input. The baseline's record `My infringement` is built here from plain
-- inputs, one per fact; a field the question's rule does not read gets a fixed placeholder.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md, "Q&A layer (seat and situations as parameters)".

§ `Fines, Penalties and Infringement Notices Enforcement Act 1994 (WA) -- the questions people ask`

§§ `Who is asking, and the shape of the answers`

DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `I have been given an infringement notice`
    `I have been fined by a court`

DECLARE `Yes or no` IS ONE OF
    yes
    no
    `does not arise for you`

DECLARE `Amount` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    amount HAS dollars IS A NUMBER

-- The baseline's `How many days the step gives me` answers 0 where this Act sets no period (the infringement notice's
-- own period is the principal enactment's; a licence suspension order runs until cancelled, s 19(9)(b)).
DECLARE `Days` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    days HAS `number of days` IS A NUMBER
    `no period is set by this Act`

-- The baseline's `the protected value` answers -1 for a kind protected whatever its value and 0 for none (r 8).
DECLARE `Protection` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `protected up to` HAS dollars IS A NUMBER
    `protected whatever its value`
    `not protected`

§§ `Carrying the baseline's answers`

GIVEN `it holds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`yes if` `it holds` MEANS
    IF `it holds` THEN yes ELSE no

GIVEN `the number` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`as an amount` `the number` MEANS amount `the number`

GIVEN `the number` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Days`
`as days` `the number` MEANS
    IF `the number` EQUALS 0 THEN `no period is set by this Act` ELSE days `the number`

GIVEN `the number` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Protection`
`as protection` `the number` MEANS
    IF `the number` EQUALS -1
    THEN `protected whatever its value`
    ELSE IF `the number` EQUALS 0
         THEN `not protected`
         ELSE `protected up to` `the number`

-- The baseline's record, from plain inputs, in the order of its fields. Each question passes its own inputs for the
-- fields its rule reads, and a fixed placeholder for the others (0, FALSE, `a law not listed in Schedule 1`, `the
-- infringement notice`, `Major Cities of Australia`), which that rule never reads.
GIVEN `p0` IS A NUMBER
      `p1` IS AN `Issuing law`
      `p2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `p3` IS A BOOLEAN
      `p4` IS A Stage
      `p5` IS A NUMBER
      `p6` IS A BOOLEAN
      `p7` IS A NUMBER
      `p8` IS A BOOLEAN
      `p9` IS A BOOLEAN
      `p10` IS A BOOLEAN
      `p11` IS A BOOLEAN
      `p12` IS A BOOLEAN
      `p13` IS A BOOLEAN
      `p14` IS AN `ASGS remoteness class`
      `p15` IS A BOOLEAN
      `p16` IS A BOOLEAN
      `p17` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `My infringement`
`the infringement from` `p0` `p1` `p2` `p3` `p4` `p5` `p6` `p7` `p8` `p9` `p10` `p11` `p12` `p13` `p14` `p15` `p16` `p17` MEANS `My infringement` WITH
    `my age at the time of the offence` IS `p0`
    `the law it was issued under` IS `p1`
    `the prosecuting authority is approved by the Registrar` IS `p2`
    `I was paying it by road traffic instalments` IS `p3`
    `the stage reached` IS `p4`
    `days since the latest document was issued` IS `p5`
    `the time to pay the notice or my next instalment has run out` IS `p6`
    `the modified penalty still unpaid` IS `p7`
    `I have paid it all` IS `p8`
    `I have paid part of it` IS `p9`
    `I have elected to go to court` IS `p10`
    `the notice or the proceedings have been withdrawn` IS `p11`
    `the time limit for prosecuting has passed` IS `p12`
    `a time to pay order has been made` IS `p13`
    `my address ASGS class` IS `p14`
    `my postcode is shared with a regional or remote area` IS `p15`
    `my address is in the metropolitan region` IS `p16`
    `my postcode is shared with the metropolitan region` IS `p17`

§§ `The stage a question arises at (design D8)`

-- Each lists every value of `Stage`, with no OTHERWISE (graffiti finding 31).
GIVEN `the stage` IS A Stage
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a final demand is the next step after` `the stage` IF
    CONSIDER `the stage`
    WHEN `the infringement notice` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a final demand` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an order to pay or elect` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a notice of intention to enforce` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a licence suspension order` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an enforcement warrant` THEN FALSE

GIVEN `the stage` IS A Stage
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `registration is the next step after` `the stage` IF
    CONSIDER `the stage`
    WHEN `the infringement notice` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a final demand` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an order to pay or elect` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a notice of intention to enforce` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a licence suspension order` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an enforcement warrant` THEN FALSE

GIVEN `the stage` IS A Stage
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a notice of intention to enforce is the next step after` `the stage` IF
    CONSIDER `the stage`
    WHEN `the infringement notice` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a final demand` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an order to pay or elect` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a notice of intention to enforce` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a licence suspension order` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an enforcement warrant` THEN FALSE

GIVEN `the stage` IS A Stage
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `licence suspension is the next step after` `the stage` IF
    CONSIDER `the stage`
    WHEN `the infringement notice` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a final demand` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an order to pay or elect` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a notice of intention to enforce` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a licence suspension order` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an enforcement warrant` THEN FALSE

GIVEN `the stage` IS A Stage
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a licence suspension order has been made, by` `the stage` IF
    CONSIDER `the stage`
    WHEN `the infringement notice` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a final demand` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an order to pay or elect` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a notice of intention to enforce` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a licence suspension order` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an enforcement warrant` THEN FALSE

GIVEN `the stage` IS A Stage
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a warrant is the next step after` `the stage` IF
    CONSIDER `the stage`
    WHEN `the infringement notice` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a final demand` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an order to pay or elect` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a notice of intention to enforce` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a licence suspension order` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an enforcement warrant` THEN FALSE

GIVEN `the stage` IS A Stage
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the notice is registered, by` `the stage` IF
    CONSIDER `the stage`
    WHEN `the infringement notice` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a final demand` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an order to pay or elect` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a notice of intention to enforce` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a licence suspension order` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an enforcement warrant` THEN TRUE

GIVEN `the stage` IS A Stage
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act's election is open, by` `the stage` IF
    CONSIDER `the stage`
    WHEN `the infringement notice` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a final demand` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an order to pay or elect` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a notice of intention to enforce` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a licence suspension order` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an enforcement warrant` THEN TRUE

GIVEN `the stage` IS A Stage
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an enforcement warrant has been issued, by` `the stage` IF
    CONSIDER `the stage`
    WHEN `the infringement notice` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a final demand` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an order to pay or elect` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a notice of intention to enforce` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a licence suspension order` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an enforcement warrant` THEN TRUE

§§ `For the person given an infringement notice (the baseline's seat, Part 3)`

-- Each question calls the baseline's function of the same subject (fpine-infringements.l4) and restates no rule: for
-- this role, and where its situation holds, its answer is the baseline's, carried in the answer types above. The
-- baseline's `My infringement` record is built here from plain inputs; a field the question's rule does not read gets a
-- fixed placeholder (`the infringement from`, above).

§§§ `ss 12, 14, 14A, 15-17A -- does Part 3 apply, the final demand and registration`

@export Does Part 3 of the Fines, Penalties and Infringement Notices Enforcement Act 1994 (WA) apply to my infringement notice (s 12)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my age at the time of the offence` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in years when the offence was alleged to have been committed
      `the law it was issued under` IS AN `Issuing law` @desc The law the infringement notice was issued under: the Road Traffic (Administration) Act 2008, another law listed in Schedule 1 of the regulations, or a law not listed there
      `the prosecuting authority is approved by the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the body that issued the notice (for example WA Police or a local government) is a prosecuting authority approved by the Registrar (s 13(1))
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does Part 3 of the Act apply to my infringement notice` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I have been given an infringement notice` THEN `yes if` (`Does Part 3 apply to my infringement notice` (`the infringement from` `my age at the time of the offence` `the law it was issued under` `the prosecuting authority is approved by the Registrar` FALSE `the infringement notice` 0 FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `Major Cities of Australia` FALSE FALSE FALSE))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can a final demand be issued to me for my unpaid infringement notice (Fines, Penalties and Infringement Notices Enforcement Act 1994 (WA) ss 14, 14A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the latest document I have been given` IS A Stage @desc The latest document you have been given about the infringement: the infringement notice itself, a final demand, an order to pay or elect (or a balance payment order), a notice of intention to enforce, a licence suspension order, or an enforcement warrant
      `my age at the time of the offence` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in years when the offence was alleged to have been committed
      `the law it was issued under` IS AN `Issuing law` @desc The law the infringement notice was issued under: the Road Traffic (Administration) Act 2008, another law listed in Schedule 1 of the regulations, or a law not listed there
      `the prosecuting authority is approved by the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the body that issued the notice (for example WA Police or a local government) is a prosecuting authority approved by the Registrar (s 13(1))
      `I have paid it all` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have paid the modified penalty and fees in full
      `the notice or the proceedings have been withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the infringement notice, or the Part 3 proceedings, have been withdrawn
      `the time to pay the notice or my next instalment has run out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the time to pay the infringement notice, or your next road-traffic instalment, has run out
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can a final demand be issued to me for my unpaid notice` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I have been given an infringement notice` THEN
        IF `a final demand is the next step after` `the latest document I have been given`
        THEN `yes if` (`Can a final demand be issued to me` (`the infringement from` `my age at the time of the offence` `the law it was issued under` `the prosecuting authority is approved by the Registrar` FALSE `the latest document I have been given` 0 `the time to pay the notice or my next instalment has run out` 0 `I have paid it all` FALSE FALSE `the notice or the proceedings have been withdrawn` FALSE FALSE `Major Cities of Australia` FALSE FALSE FALSE))
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How many days does each step under Part 3 give me to act before the next step can be taken (Fines, Penalties and Infringement Notices Enforcement Act 1994 (WA) ss 14(4), 17(3), 18(4), 101AA(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the latest document I have been given` IS A Stage @desc The latest document you have been given about the infringement: the infringement notice itself, a final demand, an order to pay or elect (or a balance payment order), a notice of intention to enforce, a licence suspension order, or an enforcement warrant
GIVETH A `Days`
`How many days does this step give me to act` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I have been given an infringement notice` THEN `as days` (`How many days the step gives me` `the latest document I have been given`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can my infringement notice be registered with the Fines Enforcement Registry (Fines, Penalties and Infringement Notices Enforcement Act 1994 (WA) ss 15, 16)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the latest document I have been given` IS A Stage @desc The latest document you have been given about the infringement: the infringement notice itself, a final demand, an order to pay or elect (or a balance payment order), a notice of intention to enforce, a licence suspension order, or an enforcement warrant
      `my age at the time of the offence` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in years when the offence was alleged to have been committed
      `the law it was issued under` IS AN `Issuing law` @desc The law the infringement notice was issued under: the Road Traffic (Administration) Act 2008, another law listed in Schedule 1 of the regulations, or a law not listed there
      `the prosecuting authority is approved by the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the body that issued the notice (for example WA Police or a local government) is a prosecuting authority approved by the Registrar (s 13(1))
      `I have paid it all` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have paid the modified penalty and fees in full
      `the notice or the proceedings have been withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the infringement notice, or the Part 3 proceedings, have been withdrawn
      `days since the latest document was issued` IS A NUMBER @desc Whole days since the date of issue of the latest document you were given
      `I have elected to go to court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have elected to have the charge heard and decided by a court
      `the time limit for prosecuting has passed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the time limit for prosecuting the offence has passed
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can my infringement notice be registered with the Fines Enforcement Registry` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I have been given an infringement notice` THEN
        IF `registration is the next step after` `the latest document I have been given`
        THEN `yes if` (`Can my infringement notice be registered` (`the infringement from` `my age at the time of the offence` `the law it was issued under` `the prosecuting authority is approved by the Registrar` FALSE `the latest document I have been given` `days since the latest document was issued` FALSE 0 `I have paid it all` FALSE `I have elected to go to court` `the notice or the proceedings have been withdrawn` `the time limit for prosecuting has passed` FALSE `Major Cities of Australia` FALSE FALSE FALSE))
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 11, Schedule 2 Division 1 -- the enforcement fees and what I must pay now`

@export What enforcement fees have been added to my infringement by the stage it has reached (Fines, Penalties and Infringement Notices Enforcement Regulations 1994 (WA) r 9, Schedule 2 Division 1)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the latest document I have been given` IS A Stage @desc The latest document you have been given about the infringement: the infringement notice itself, a final demand, an order to pay or elect (or a balance payment order), a notice of intention to enforce, a licence suspension order, or an enforcement warrant
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What enforcement fees have been added to my infringement` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I have been given an infringement notice` THEN `as an amount` (`What enforcement fees have been added` `the latest document I have been given`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How much must I pay now to settle my infringement (Fines, Penalties and Infringement Notices Enforcement Act 1994 (WA) ss 11, 14(4), 17(3), Schedule 2)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the latest document I have been given` IS A Stage @desc The latest document you have been given about the infringement: the infringement notice itself, a final demand, an order to pay or elect (or a balance payment order), a notice of intention to enforce, a licence suspension order, or an enforcement warrant
      `I have paid it all` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have paid the modified penalty and fees in full
      `the notice or the proceedings have been withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the infringement notice, or the Part 3 proceedings, have been withdrawn
      `the modified penalty still unpaid` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of the modified penalty (the amount the infringement notice asks for), or of its outstanding balance, is unpaid, in dollars
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`How much must I pay now to settle my infringement` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I have been given an infringement notice` THEN `as an amount` (`What must I pay now` (`the infringement from` 0 `a law not listed in Schedule 1` FALSE FALSE `the latest document I have been given` 0 FALSE `the modified penalty still unpaid` `I have paid it all` FALSE FALSE `the notice or the proceedings have been withdrawn` FALSE FALSE `Major Cities of Australia` FALSE FALSE FALSE))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 14(4)(b), 21, 23, 26 -- electing to go to court, and being taken to be convicted`

@export Can I still elect to have the charge heard and decided by a court instead of paying (Fines, Penalties and Infringement Notices Enforcement Act 1994 (WA) ss 14(4)(b), 21)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the latest document I have been given` IS A Stage @desc The latest document you have been given about the infringement: the infringement notice itself, a final demand, an order to pay or elect (or a balance payment order), a notice of intention to enforce, a licence suspension order, or an enforcement warrant
      `my age at the time of the offence` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in years when the offence was alleged to have been committed
      `the law it was issued under` IS AN `Issuing law` @desc The law the infringement notice was issued under: the Road Traffic (Administration) Act 2008, another law listed in Schedule 1 of the regulations, or a law not listed there
      `the prosecuting authority is approved by the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the body that issued the notice (for example WA Police or a local government) is a prosecuting authority approved by the Registrar (s 13(1))
      `I have paid it all` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have paid the modified penalty and fees in full
      `the notice or the proceedings have been withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the infringement notice, or the Part 3 proceedings, have been withdrawn
      `I was paying it by road traffic instalments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you paid a first instalment under the Road Traffic (Administration) Act 2008 Part 5 instalment scheme and then missed one (s 14A)
      `I have elected to go to court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have elected to have the charge heard and decided by a court
      `I have paid part of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have paid any part of the modified penalty or fees (even by a payment later dishonoured)
      `a time to pay order has been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Registrar has made a time to pay order for this infringement notice
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I still elect to have the charge heard by a court` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I have been given an infringement notice` THEN
        IF `the Act's election is open, by` `the latest document I have been given`
        THEN `yes if` (`Can I elect to go to court` (`the infringement from` `my age at the time of the offence` `the law it was issued under` `the prosecuting authority is approved by the Registrar` `I was paying it by road traffic instalments` `the latest document I have been given` 0 FALSE 0 `I have paid it all` `I have paid part of it` `I have elected to go to court` `the notice or the proceedings have been withdrawn` FALSE `a time to pay order has been made` `Major Cities of Australia` FALSE FALSE FALSE))
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Am I taken to be convicted of the offence for the purposes of the Road Traffic (Authorisation to Drive) Act 2008 s 16(1)(a) (Fines, Penalties and Infringement Notices Enforcement Act 1994 (WA) ss 23, 26)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the latest document I have been given` IS A Stage @desc The latest document you have been given about the infringement: the infringement notice itself, a final demand, an order to pay or elect (or a balance payment order), a notice of intention to enforce, a licence suspension order, or an enforcement warrant
      `my age at the time of the offence` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in years when the offence was alleged to have been committed
      `the law it was issued under` IS AN `Issuing law` @desc The law the infringement notice was issued under: the Road Traffic (Administration) Act 2008, another law listed in Schedule 1 of the regulations, or a law not listed there
      `the prosecuting authority is approved by the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the body that issued the notice (for example WA Police or a local government) is a prosecuting authority approved by the Registrar (s 13(1))
      `I was paying it by road traffic instalments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you paid a first instalment under the Road Traffic (Administration) Act 2008 Part 5 instalment scheme and then missed one (s 14A)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I taken to be convicted for driver licensing` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I have been given an infringement notice` THEN `yes if` (`Am I taken to be convicted for driver licensing` (`the infringement from` `my age at the time of the offence` `the law it was issued under` `the prosecuting authority is approved by the Registrar` `I was paying it by road traffic instalments` `the latest document I have been given` 0 FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `Major Cities of Australia` FALSE FALSE FALSE))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 18-20A, 21H, r 2B -- the notice of intention to enforce and licence suspension`

@export Is my address in a remote area for the Fines, Penalties and Infringement Notices Enforcement Act 1994 (WA) (s 4B; Fines, Penalties and Infringement Notices Enforcement Regulations 1994 (WA) r 2B)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my address ASGS class` IS AN `ASGS remoteness class` @desc The remoteness class of your address under the ABS Australian Statistical Geography Standard (2016): Major Cities, Inner Regional, Outer Regional, Remote or Very Remote Australia
      `my postcode is shared with a regional or remote area` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your postcode is shared with an area classed as Inner Regional, Outer Regional, Remote or Very Remote Australia
      `my address is in the metropolitan region` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your address is in the metropolitan region (Perth)
      `my postcode is shared with the metropolitan region` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your postcode is shared with an area in the metropolitan region
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my address in a remote area for this Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I have been given an infringement notice` THEN `yes if` (`Is my address in a remote area` (`the infringement from` 0 `a law not listed in Schedule 1` FALSE FALSE `the infringement notice` 0 FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `my address ASGS class` `my postcode is shared with a regional or remote area` `my address is in the metropolitan region` `my postcode is shared with the metropolitan region`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can a notice of intention to enforce be issued to me (Fines, Penalties and Infringement Notices Enforcement Act 1994 (WA) ss 18, 21H)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the latest document I have been given` IS A Stage @desc The latest document you have been given about the infringement: the infringement notice itself, a final demand, an order to pay or elect (or a balance payment order), a notice of intention to enforce, a licence suspension order, or an enforcement warrant
      `my age at the time of the offence` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in years when the offence was alleged to have been committed
      `the law it was issued under` IS AN `Issuing law` @desc The law the infringement notice was issued under: the Road Traffic (Administration) Act 2008, another law listed in Schedule 1 of the regulations, or a law not listed there
      `the prosecuting authority is approved by the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the body that issued the notice (for example WA Police or a local government) is a prosecuting authority approved by the Registrar (s 13(1))
      `I have paid it all` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have paid the modified penalty and fees in full
      `the notice or the proceedings have been withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the infringement notice, or the Part 3 proceedings, have been withdrawn
      `days since the latest document was issued` IS A NUMBER @desc Whole days since the date of issue of the latest document you were given
      `I have elected to go to court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have elected to have the charge heard and decided by a court
      `a time to pay order has been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Registrar has made a time to pay order for this infringement notice
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can a notice of intention to enforce be issued to me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I have been given an infringement notice` THEN
        IF `a notice of intention to enforce is the next step after` `the latest document I have been given`
        THEN `yes if` (`Can a notice of intention to enforce be issued to me` (`the infringement from` `my age at the time of the offence` `the law it was issued under` `the prosecuting authority is approved by the Registrar` FALSE `the latest document I have been given` `days since the latest document was issued` FALSE 0 `I have paid it all` FALSE `I have elected to go to court` `the notice or the proceedings have been withdrawn` FALSE `a time to pay order has been made` `Major Cities of Australia` FALSE FALSE FALSE))
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can my driver's licence (or vehicle licence) be suspended for not paying my infringement (Fines, Penalties and Infringement Notices Enforcement Act 1994 (WA) ss 19, 21H)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the latest document I have been given` IS A Stage @desc The latest document you have been given about the infringement: the infringement notice itself, a final demand, an order to pay or elect (or a balance payment order), a notice of intention to enforce, a licence suspension order, or an enforcement warrant
      `my age at the time of the offence` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in years when the offence was alleged to have been committed
      `the law it was issued under` IS AN `Issuing law` @desc The law the infringement notice was issued under: the Road Traffic (Administration) Act 2008, another law listed in Schedule 1 of the regulations, or a law not listed there
      `the prosecuting authority is approved by the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the body that issued the notice (for example WA Police or a local government) is a prosecuting authority approved by the Registrar (s 13(1))
      `I have paid it all` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have paid the modified penalty and fees in full
      `the notice or the proceedings have been withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the infringement notice, or the Part 3 proceedings, have been withdrawn
      `I have elected to go to court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have elected to have the charge heard and decided by a court
      `a time to pay order has been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Registrar has made a time to pay order for this infringement notice
      `my address ASGS class` IS AN `ASGS remoteness class` @desc The remoteness class of your address under the ABS Australian Statistical Geography Standard (2016): Major Cities, Inner Regional, Outer Regional, Remote or Very Remote Australia
      `my postcode is shared with a regional or remote area` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your postcode is shared with an area classed as Inner Regional, Outer Regional, Remote or Very Remote Australia
      `my address is in the metropolitan region` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your address is in the metropolitan region (Perth)
      `my postcode is shared with the metropolitan region` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your postcode is shared with an area in the metropolitan region
      `the Registrar has reasonable grounds to believe s 20A(3) would apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have given the Registrar information about your circumstances (urgent medical treatment, your principal means of earning income, or serious hindrance of family or personal responsibilities) that gives reasonable grounds to believe the s 20A(3) grounds would apply
      `the due date in the notice has passed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the due date stated in the notice of intention to enforce has passed
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can my driver's licence be suspended for not paying` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I have been given an infringement notice` THEN
        IF `licence suspension is the next step after` `the latest document I have been given`
        THEN `yes if` (`Can my licence be suspended` (`the infringement from` `my age at the time of the offence` `the law it was issued under` `the prosecuting authority is approved by the Registrar` FALSE `the latest document I have been given` 0 FALSE 0 `I have paid it all` FALSE `I have elected to go to court` `the notice or the proceedings have been withdrawn` FALSE `a time to pay order has been made` `my address ASGS class` `my postcode is shared with a regional or remote area` `my address is in the metropolitan region` `my postcode is shared with the metropolitan region`) `the Registrar has reasonable grounds to believe s 20A(3) would apply` `the due date in the notice has passed`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can I ask the Registrar to cancel the licence suspension order made against me (Fines, Penalties and Infringement Notices Enforcement Act 1994 (WA) s 20A(1)-(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the latest document I have been given` IS A Stage @desc The latest document you have been given about the infringement: the infringement notice itself, a final demand, an order to pay or elect (or a balance payment order), a notice of intention to enforce, a licence suspension order, or an enforcement warrant
      `I have elected to go to court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have elected to have the charge heard and decided by a court
      `it deprives me of urgent medical treatment for me or my family` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the suspension takes away your means of getting urgent medical treatment for an illness, disease or disability that you or a family member is known to have
      `it deprives me of my principal means of earning income to pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the suspension takes away your principal means of earning the income to pay what you owe
      `it seriously hinders my family or personal responsibilities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the suspension seriously hinders you in performing family or personal responsibilities
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I ask the Registrar to cancel my licence suspension order` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I have been given an infringement notice` THEN
        IF `a licence suspension order has been made, by` `the latest document I have been given`
        THEN `yes if` (`Can I ask the Registrar to cancel my licence suspension` (`the infringement from` 0 `a law not listed in Schedule 1` FALSE FALSE `the latest document I have been given` 0 FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE `I have elected to go to court` FALSE FALSE FALSE `Major Cities of Australia` FALSE FALSE FALSE) `it deprives me of urgent medical treatment for me or my family` `it deprives me of my principal means of earning income to pay` `it seriously hinders my family or personal responsibilities`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must the licence suspension order made against me be cancelled (Fines, Penalties and Infringement Notices Enforcement Act 1994 (WA) ss 20(1), (2A), 20A(5), 21H(1), 22(4)(b))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the latest document I have been given` IS A Stage @desc The latest document you have been given about the infringement: the infringement notice itself, a final demand, an order to pay or elect (or a balance payment order), a notice of intention to enforce, a licence suspension order, or an enforcement warrant
      `I have paid it all` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have paid the modified penalty and fees in full
      `I have elected to go to court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have elected to have the charge heard and decided by a court
      `the notice or the proceedings have been withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the infringement notice, or the Part 3 proceedings, have been withdrawn
      `a time to pay order has been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Registrar has made a time to pay order for this infringement notice
      `I gave notice that my current address is in a remote area` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have given the Registrar the approved-form notice that your current address is in a remote area
      `the Registrar is satisfied s 20A(3) applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Registrar is satisfied, on your request, that one of the s 20A(3) grounds applies to you
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must the licence suspension order made against me be cancelled` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I have been given an infringement notice` THEN
        IF `a licence suspension order has been made, by` `the latest document I have been given`
        THEN `yes if` (`Must my licence suspension be cancelled` (`the infringement from` 0 `a law not listed in Schedule 1` FALSE FALSE `the latest document I have been given` 0 FALSE 0 `I have paid it all` FALSE `I have elected to go to court` `the notice or the proceedings have been withdrawn` FALSE `a time to pay order has been made` `Major Cities of Australia` FALSE FALSE FALSE) `I gave notice that my current address is in a remote area` `the Registrar is satisfied s 20A(3) applies to me`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 21B, 21C -- time to pay orders`

@export Can I apply to the Registrar for a time to pay order (Fines, Penalties and Infringement Notices Enforcement Act 1994 (WA) s 21B)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the latest document I have been given` IS A Stage @desc The latest document you have been given about the infringement: the infringement notice itself, a final demand, an order to pay or elect (or a balance payment order), a notice of intention to enforce, a licence suspension order, or an enforcement warrant
      `I have paid it all` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have paid the modified penalty and fees in full
      `the notice or the proceedings have been withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the infringement notice, or the Part 3 proceedings, have been withdrawn
      `I have elected to go to court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have elected to have the charge heard and decided by a court
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I apply to the Registrar for a time to pay order` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I have been given an infringement notice` THEN
        IF `the notice is registered, by` `the latest document I have been given`
        THEN `yes if` (`Can I apply for a time to pay order` (`the infringement from` 0 `a law not listed in Schedule 1` FALSE FALSE `the latest document I have been given` 0 FALSE 0 `I have paid it all` FALSE `I have elected to go to court` `the notice or the proceedings have been withdrawn` FALSE FALSE `Major Cities of Australia` FALSE FALSE FALSE))
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must the Registrar give me a time to pay order on my application (Fines, Penalties and Infringement Notices Enforcement Act 1994 (WA) s 21C(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the latest document I have been given` IS A Stage @desc The latest document you have been given about the infringement: the infringement notice itself, a final demand, an order to pay or elect (or a balance payment order), a notice of intention to enforce, a licence suspension order, or an enforcement warrant
      `I have paid it all` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have paid the modified penalty and fees in full
      `the notice or the proceedings have been withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the infringement notice, or the Part 3 proceedings, have been withdrawn
      `I have elected to go to court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have elected to have the charge heard and decided by a court
      `the Registrar is satisfied I cannot pay within 28 days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Registrar is satisfied you do not have the means to pay the whole unpaid amount within 28 days after you apply
      `the Registrar is satisfied my offer is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Registrar is satisfied your offer to pay by a set date or by regular instalments is reasonable
      `I have broken a time to pay order before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have previously contravened a time to pay order under this Act (for any infringement or fine)
      `the Registrar is satisfied I had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you have broken one before: whether the Registrar is satisfied there was a reasonable excuse
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must the Registrar give me a time to pay order` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I have been given an infringement notice` THEN
        IF `the notice is registered, by` `the latest document I have been given`
        THEN `yes if` (`Must the Registrar give me a time to pay order` (`the infringement from` 0 `a law not listed in Schedule 1` FALSE FALSE `the latest document I have been given` 0 FALSE 0 `I have paid it all` FALSE `I have elected to go to court` `the notice or the proceedings have been withdrawn` FALSE FALSE `Major Cities of Australia` FALSE FALSE FALSE) `the Registrar is satisfied I cannot pay within 28 days` `the Registrar is satisfied my offer is reasonable` `I have broken a time to pay order before` `the Registrar is satisfied I had a reasonable excuse`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 21A, 68B, 75, 101AA, r 8 -- the enforcement warrant, and what the Sheriff cannot seize`

@export Can an enforcement warrant be issued against me (Fines, Penalties and Infringement Notices Enforcement Act 1994 (WA) ss 21A, 21H)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the latest document I have been given` IS A Stage @desc The latest document you have been given about the infringement: the infringement notice itself, a final demand, an order to pay or elect (or a balance payment order), a notice of intention to enforce, a licence suspension order, or an enforcement warrant
      `my age at the time of the offence` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in years when the offence was alleged to have been committed
      `the law it was issued under` IS AN `Issuing law` @desc The law the infringement notice was issued under: the Road Traffic (Administration) Act 2008, another law listed in Schedule 1 of the regulations, or a law not listed there
      `the prosecuting authority is approved by the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the body that issued the notice (for example WA Police or a local government) is a prosecuting authority approved by the Registrar (s 13(1))
      `I have paid it all` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have paid the modified penalty and fees in full
      `the notice or the proceedings have been withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the infringement notice, or the Part 3 proceedings, have been withdrawn
      `I have elected to go to court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have elected to have the charge heard and decided by a court
      `a time to pay order has been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Registrar has made a time to pay order for this infringement notice
      `the due date in the notice has passed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the due date stated in the notice of intention to enforce has passed
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can an enforcement warrant be issued against me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I have been given an infringement notice` THEN
        IF `a warrant is the next step after` `the latest document I have been given`
        THEN `yes if` (`Can an enforcement warrant be issued against me` (`the infringement from` `my age at the time of the offence` `the law it was issued under` `the prosecuting authority is approved by the Registrar` FALSE `the latest document I have been given` 0 FALSE 0 `I have paid it all` FALSE `I have elected to go to court` `the notice or the proceedings have been withdrawn` FALSE `a time to pay order has been made` `Major Cities of Australia` FALSE FALSE FALSE) `the due date in the notice has passed`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can the Magistrates Court cancel the enforcement warrant issued against me (Fines, Penalties and Infringement Notices Enforcement Act 1994 (WA) ss 68B, 101AA)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the latest document I have been given` IS A Stage @desc The latest document you have been given about the infringement: the infringement notice itself, a final demand, an order to pay or elect (or a balance payment order), a notice of intention to enforce, a licence suspension order, or an enforcement warrant
      `days since the Sheriff's s 68B notice` IS A NUMBER @desc Whole days since the Sheriff gave you the notice of your right to apply to cancel the warrant
      `I applied before and was refused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you already applied to cancel this or another warrant for the same infringement notice and were refused
      `I received none of the notices` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you received none of: the infringement notice, the final demand, the order to pay or elect (or balance payment order), the notice of intention to enforce, and any notice confirming licence suspension
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can the Magistrates Court cancel the enforcement warrant issued against me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I have been given an infringement notice` THEN
        IF `an enforcement warrant has been issued, by` `the latest document I have been given`
        THEN `yes if` (`Can the Magistrates Court cancel my warrant` `days since the Sheriff's s 68B notice` `I applied before and was refused` `I received none of the notices`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Up to what value is property of this kind protected from seizure under an enforcement warrant (Fines, Penalties and Infringement Notices Enforcement Act 1994 (WA) s 75; Fines, Penalties and Infringement Notices Enforcement Regulations 1994 (WA) r 8)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the latest document I have been given` IS A Stage @desc The latest document you have been given about the infringement: the infringement notice itself, a final demand, an order to pay or elect (or a balance payment order), a notice of intention to enforce, a licence suspension order, or an enforcement warrant
      `the kind` IS A `Property kind` @desc What the property is
GIVETH A `Protection`
`Up to what value is my property of this kind protected from seizure` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I have been given an infringement notice` THEN
        IF `an enforcement warrant has been issued, by` `the latest document I have been given`
        THEN `as protection` (`the protected value` `the kind`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can the Sheriff seize this property of mine under an enforcement warrant (Fines, Penalties and Infringement Notices Enforcement Act 1994 (WA) s 75; Fines, Penalties and Infringement Notices Enforcement Regulations 1994 (WA) r 8)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the latest document I have been given` IS A Stage @desc The latest document you have been given about the infringement: the infringement notice itself, a final demand, an order to pay or elect (or a balance payment order), a notice of intention to enforce, a licence suspension order, or an enforcement warrant
      `the kind` IS A `Property kind` @desc What the property is
      `its value` IS A NUMBER @desc Its value in dollars
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can the Sheriff seize this property of mine under the warrant` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I have been given an infringement notice` THEN
        IF `an enforcement warrant has been issued, by` `the latest document I have been given`
        THEN `yes if` (`Can the Sheriff seize it` `the kind` `its value`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 22, 24, 46A-46C -- withdrawal, paying in full, and work and development permits`

@export How much must be refunded to me if the prosecuting authority withdraws (Fines, Penalties and Infringement Notices Enforcement Act 1994 (WA) s 22(5)(a))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the proceedings were withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the prosecuting authority has withdrawn the Part 3 proceedings by a notice of withdrawal
      `what I paid under Part 3` IS A NUMBER @desc How much you paid under Part 3 for this offence, in dollars
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`How much must be refunded to me now the proceedings are withdrawn` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I have been given an infringement notice` THEN
        IF `the proceedings were withdrawn`
        THEN `as an amount` (`How much must be refunded to me` `the proceedings were withdrawn` `what I paid under Part 3`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export If I pay in full under Part 3, am I protected from any further prosecution or penalty that a conviction would bar (Fines, Penalties and Infringement Notices Enforcement Act 1994 (WA) s 24(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have paid it all` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have paid the modified penalty and fees in full
      `the notice or the proceedings have been withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the infringement notice, or the Part 3 proceedings, have been withdrawn
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`If I pay in full, am I protected from further prosecution` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I have been given an infringement notice` THEN `yes if` (`Am I protected from further prosecution` (`the infringement from` 0 `a law not listed in Schedule 1` FALSE FALSE `the infringement notice` 0 FALSE 0 `I have paid it all` FALSE FALSE `the notice or the proceedings have been withdrawn` FALSE FALSE `Major Cities of Australia` FALSE FALSE FALSE))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- Settled on the role alone: a work and development permit is for a court fine (s 28(1), s 46C), never for an
-- infringement notice (finding 1). The baseline is asked with the debt an infringement notice; its two other inputs are
-- not read for that debt and get FALSE as placeholders.
@export Can an approved sponsor apply for a work and development permit for my unpaid infringement notice (Fines, Penalties and Infringement Notices Enforcement Act 1994 (WA) ss 28(1), 46B, 46C)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can an approved sponsor apply for a work and development permit for my infringement` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I have been given an infringement notice` THEN `yes if` (`Can a sponsor apply for a work and development permit for me` `an unpaid infringement notice under Part 3` FALSE FALSE)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the person fined by a court (Part 4 and Part 7)`

-- A court fine is a Part 4 fine (s 28(1)). The baseline encodes of Part 4 only the work and development permit (ss 4A,
-- 46A-46C); Part 7, and so s 75 with r 8, applies to a warrant issued under Part 3, 4 or 6 (s 63, "warrant").

§§§ `ss 4A, 46A-46C -- work and development permits`

@export Can an approved sponsor apply for a work and development permit for my court fine (Fines, Penalties and Infringement Notices Enforcement Act 1994 (WA) ss 4A, 46B, 46C)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am experiencing hardship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are experiencing hardship (s 4A): financial hardship that affects your capacity to pay, family violence, mental illness, disability, homelessness, alcohol or drug problems, or another kind
      `a Part 4 notice of intention to enforce has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a notice of intention to enforce the fine has been issued under s 42
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can an approved sponsor apply for a work and development permit for my court fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I have been fined by a court` THEN `yes if` (`Can a sponsor apply for a work and development permit for me` `a court fine registered under Part 4` `I am experiencing hardship` `a Part 4 notice of intention to enforce has been issued`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can a work and development permit for my court fine include a mentoring programme (Fines, Penalties and Infringement Notices Enforcement Act 1994 (WA) s 46A(e))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my age when the permit is issued` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in years when the permit would be issued
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can a work and development permit for my court fine include a mentoring programme` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I have been fined by a court` THEN `yes if` (`Can my permit include mentoring` `my age when the permit is issued`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `Part 7 -- what the Sheriff cannot seize`

@export Up to what value is property of this kind protected from seizure under an enforcement warrant for my fine (Fines, Penalties and Infringement Notices Enforcement Act 1994 (WA) ss 63, 75; Fines, Penalties and Infringement Notices Enforcement Regulations 1994 (WA) r 8)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `an enforcement warrant has been issued against me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an enforcement warrant has been issued against you for the fine (Part 7)
      `the kind` IS A `Property kind` @desc What the property is
GIVETH A `Protection`
`Up to what value is my property of this kind protected from seizure for my fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I have been fined by a court` THEN
        IF `an enforcement warrant has been issued against me`
        THEN `as protection` (`the protected value` `the kind`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can the Sheriff seize this property of mine under an enforcement warrant for my fine (Fines, Penalties and Infringement Notices Enforcement Act 1994 (WA) ss 63, 75; Fines, Penalties and Infringement Notices Enforcement Regulations 1994 (WA) r 8)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `an enforcement warrant has been issued against me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an enforcement warrant has been issued against you for the fine (Part 7)
      `the kind` IS A `Property kind` @desc What the property is
      `its value` IS A NUMBER @desc Its value in dollars
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can the Sheriff seize this property of mine for my fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I have been fined by a court` THEN
        IF `an enforcement warrant has been issued against me`
        THEN `yes if` (`Can the Sheriff seize it` `the kind` `its value`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`
